---
title: Tzatziki
category: More
cuisine: Greek
diet:
  - vegetarian
  - gluten-free
tags:
  - sauce
servings: 6
prep time: 4 hours
cook time: 10 minutes
created: 2026-08-03
updated: 2026-08-03
---

Wash and deseed @cucumber{1}.

Coarsely grate the cucumber and place in a colander for at least ~{1%hour} to drain.

Peel and crush @garlic{2%cloves}, removing the germ for a milder flavour. You can press the minced garlic with the side of the blade or use a #mortar and pestle{} until it's ground to a paste.

Transfer @Greek yogurt{400%g} into a bowl, add @extra virgin olive oil{20%g}, @vinegar{10%g}, and @fine sea salt{} to taste. Mix well.

Press the cucumber with the back of a spoon to squeeze out any excess water then mix it in with the yogurt.

Add the garlic paste and mix well.

Transfer to the refrigerator and allow to rest for ~{2-3%hours} before serving.

Garnish with @fresh dill{} and a drizzle of olive oil.